---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/layout/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Focus Pro Terms of Service — Focus Pet"
  description="The terms for purchasing and using Focus Pro, the optional upgrade to Focus Pet."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
      <a href="/" class="font-heading font-semibold text-text-secondary no-underline hover:text-accent-blue">
        &larr; Back to Home
      </a>

      <div class="mt-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold md:text-4xl">Focus Pro Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-text-secondary">Last updated July 23, 2026.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8 text-text-secondary">
        <p>
          These terms apply specifically to Focus Pro, the optional paid upgrade to Focus Pet. They should be read
          together with the
          <a href="/terms">Focus Pet Terms of Service</a>, which cover the free application. If anything here
          conflicts with the main terms, this page governs Focus Pro specifically.
        </p>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Overview of Focus Pro</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pro is an optional upgrade to Focus Pet that gives you stronger tools for staying on task. Unlike
            the free version, Focus Pro can:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>Automatically close applications you've selected before a focus session begins.</li>
            <li>Block websites you've selected while a focus session is running.</li>
            <li>Keep those restrictions in place until your session ends, based on the settings you choose.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Everything else about Focus Pet — the focus timer, decorating your space, earning Energy — works exactly
            the same whether or not you have Focus Pro.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Subscription and Purchase Terms</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pro may be offered as a one-time purchase or a recurring subscription, depending on the option you
            choose at checkout. Pricing and billing details are shown before you complete your purchase.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you choose a subscription, it renews automatically at the end of each billing period unless you cancel
            before the renewal date. You can manage or cancel your subscription through your account settings or the
            platform you purchased through. Refunds are handled according to that platform's standard refund policy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Application Closing</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            You choose exactly which applications Focus Pro is allowed to close. Focus Pro only closes applications
            you've selected — it never closes an application you haven't added to your list, and it doesn't touch
            anything else running on your computer.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Because a selected application may close as soon as a focus session starts, you're responsible for
            saving your work before beginning a session. TryFocusPet isn't responsible for any unsaved work lost
            because a selected application was closed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Website Blocking</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            You choose which websites to block. While a focus session is running, Focus Pro attempts to prevent
            access to those websites.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            How well blocking works can vary depending on things outside our control — operating system changes,
            browser updates, administrator permissions, VPNs, antivirus software, or other third-party software
            running on your device. We can't guarantee that every website will always be blocked under every system
            configuration.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">User Responsibility</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">When you use Focus Pro, you're responsible for:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>Choosing which applications and websites to block.</li>
            <li>Reviewing your block lists before starting a session.</li>
            <li>
              Understanding that enabling blocking may interrupt your normal computer use until the session ends.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Limitations of the Software</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pro is designed to support your focus habits, not to act as an unbreakable system lock. It relies
            on standard operating system permissions to close applications and block websites, and those permissions
            can be affected by your system configuration or by other software on your device.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pro is provided as-is, without a guarantee that application closing or website blocking will work
            perfectly in every situation. We're honest about this because we'd rather set the right expectations than
            overpromise what the software can do.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">Focus Pro relies on trusted third-party services, including:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li><span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Supabase</span> — user authentication and cloud save synchronization.</li>
            <li><span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">RevenueCat</span> — subscription and purchase management.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">These services are governed by their own Terms of Service and Privacy Policies.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Updates</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We continually improve Focus Pro and may release updates, add features, adjust how application closing or
            website blocking works, or discontinue features at any time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Changes to these Terms</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We may update these terms as Focus Pro changes. If we do, we'll update the date at the top of this page.
            Continuing to use Focus Pro after an update means you accept the revised terms.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            If you have questions about these terms, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:help@tryfocuspet.com">help@tryfocuspet.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
